---
description: Chat is trip-polama's primary planner/manager interface
globs: "**/*.{ts,tsx}"
alwaysApply: true
---
# Chat-First Product

- Before trip creation, recommend sourced nearby spots and review selected stops;
  save them as waypoints in the same transaction. Never generate coordinates with an LLM.
- Mutation confirmations show labeled human-readable data, not JSON, schema keys
  or internal IDs. Read-only retrieval/calculation/navigation must not ask approval.
- Model-generated read prose is not authoritative. Retrieve/format actual saved
  records; use deterministic aggregates. Compact intent selection and known quick
  commands keep latency low. Never auto-execute a write via the read path.
- The chat image icon supports multi-select local photo batches with previews.
  Never send image bytes to models or add photo location tags.

- Split model roles: planner uses a larger online LLM with controlled research
  tools and source-backed recommendations; manager uses a lightweight local model
  for trip reads/writes, summaries and quick actions. Different prompts alone
  are not the intended split. Resource access requires actual tools.
- Existing-trip management must not silently escalate to cloud inference. Allow
  explicit online Research/Replan while preserving the same conversation.
- Planner provider/model is configured server-side through PLANNER_* settings;
  manager uses its separately configured local Ollama endpoint. Keep credentials
  out of browser code. Online gateway currently binds to loopback for development;
  do not expose publicly without auth, rate limits and deployment hardening.
- Planner research tools are bounded, allowlisted reads. Display retrieved source
  URLs/times; Wikipedia snippets are not live weather/fares/availability. Optional
  Brave search enables broader research. Do not invent tools or source provenance.
- Local manager replies allow zero or one requested action to limit unrelated
  mutations from small models. Summaries use no actions; all writes still need approval.
- Read-only local tools can run automatically; mutations require confirmation.
  Measure manager latency and keep deterministic calculations outside the model.

- Home focuses on one persistent conversation per trip; exploration can start
  before creation. Keep history through planner-to-manager transition.
- Manual screens use the same local store and stay accessible from chat.
- Model tools require strict runtime schemas, scoped execution, explicit
  confirmation/dismissal and tests. Prompts are not a security boundary.
- Never run arbitrary model code, accept model-supplied trip IDs, fabricate
  coordinates/media or bypass device permissions.
- Commit mutations and execution status atomically to prevent duplicate actions.
- Load fresh trip context before every model request, including manual edits.
- Label proposed versus completed changes; only local results prove success.
- Keep model connection explicit. Network availability does not mean readiness.
- Structured images/GPS fields are omitted from model context. User-authored
  message text is transmitted as written to the selected endpoint.
- Photos stay location-free. Embedded metadata stripping is still deferred.
